{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Versil","id":"148682928434577408","is_bot":0,"username":"versil"},"author_id":"148682928434577408","channel_id":"866464124473311282","content":"\"Hmm. Hard question. On one hand, absolutely. On the other, if we were to open all the cages, they might not find themselves at home here in the city. Maybe they can't eat things that grow here normally, maybe some beasts here would be too dangerous and they'd be unprepared. Maybe they would wander into the damn Noir.\"\n\n\"Back home we know what lives in the forest around the town, but many things here I haven't seen before. Maybe by seeing them here someone would decide to help their kind where they're at home, saving more of them. But by keeping them here, we limit their freedom. But outside might be more dangerous, and a threat to their lives. Even before landing on Mender's path, maintaining balance has always been more difficult than paying no attention to it, I suppose.\"","created_at":"2021-07-20T08:53:51.184000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"866966123039686686","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
